<p>Four astronauts arrived at the International Space Station on Saturday aboard a SpaceX Dragon capsule, bringing the orbiting lab back to a full crew after an earlier, health-related departure cut the previous rotation short. The newcomers include astronauts from the United States, France, and Russia, a reminder that the station still runs on international teamwork. The arrival comes after NASA’s first medical evacuation in 65 years of human spaceflight. One of the four astronauts SpaceX launched last summer developed what officials called a serious health issue, prompting an urgent return to Earth.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/hlndxmJa02JuIbXWiqv0LrFGVLVK4E-SFaMXP98SF6gnbarTmJeKn6Dgi3jYUF_6TIw8DQzvbBigWRyKbqkbBqvG34BRRFZwqTjqpga9VDsT8GCfhDAPz9R_9Zf8sQVPbCxJ8XrXo9JTktJtAEpa4eBHuyX0QH4UWIOElx7V45KVU3WMa7zXUk_V0qKwkLDTPgn467lQXktasPPmk1atXLUgK47O1A6lH5WCKyX2NYbNrTJ-jbiSGsvu' alt='In this image from video provided by NASA, France’s Sophie Adenot, Russia’s Andrei Fedyaev and Americans Jessica Meir and Jack Hathaway greet colleagues as they enter the International Space Station after arriving on a SpaceX Dragon capsule on Saturday, February 14, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Multinational milestone: Le Monde said the arriving crew includes French astronaut Sophie Adenot, described as France’s second woman to fly to space.</li><li>Launch-to-docking: The crew lifted off from Cape Canaveral on a Falcon 9 and reached the ISS about a day later in a SpaceX Dragon capsule, according to BBC video and other reports.</li><li>Earlier rotation cut short: The outgoing crew returned to Earth early in January after officials described a serious health issue.</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3343602/4-astronauts-arrive-international-space-station-replace-nasas-evacuated-crew'>4 astronauts arrive at International Space Station to replace Nasa’s evacuated crew</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='htt